   "translation": "Kun'yomi (Japanese 訓読み, romanised kun'yomi) is one of the ways Japanese pronounces kanji: a character is read by its meaning, using the native Japanese word that corresponds to it. It is also called wakun or jikun.",
   "note": "训读 is what made kanbun possible: a Chinese text read straight off the page as Japanese."
