   "translation": "The two kinds of reading can live side by side in one character. Take the character 山 'mountain': its on'yomi is サン (san), and its kun'yomi is やま (yama). The first comes from the Chinese sound of the character; the second answers directly to a native Japanese word (its sound owes nothing to Chinese). Some on'yomi sound close to Chinese, so they feel fairly familiar to Chinese speakers, while kun'yomi feel strange. For example, 金 'gold' has the kun'yomi かね (kane), and the on'yomi キン (kin) and コン (kon).",
